{"skill":{"slug":"file-manager","displayName":"File Manager"},"version":{"version":"1.2.0","createdAt":1774418743565,"changelog":"Add safety checks, extract shared utils, remove unimplemented features, drop external dependencies","changelogSource":"user","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"references/best_practices.md","size":1921,"sha256":"32e6276249a3932e2ff02274be41f76ef3c88e68ea71fb2e13d9330eb09aea8e","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"requirements.txt","size":106,"sha256":"e3e23d07de4f7a1793b5152d7d8ae691460418f3ea7815df68cd458115ae9d61","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/batch_rename.py","size":7412,"sha256":"b38010f07266f9bdad52f326ae09f553d1ca5c4f2863b2e58db5375e85e2c235","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/deduplicate.py","size":7207,"sha256":"73744f2f5ace3b7af1f95870e318e6cbfd5a12814f42f82f1994cfbe51e55a2c","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/organize.py","size":8004,"sha256":"260efff4203e01a906b25fd81c7cd36c67194b1b74ca50ca242d47766b241684","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/sync.py","size":6671,"sha256":"ee2d78796f063138d33bfb27b222b78ceb66d2b08f1cc7e51c3aa68010440b0b","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/utils.py","size":652,"sha256":"27bbddf2198f0450675697e83ef0b42c9f1fa90bf526296ec60579c506e68cd7","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":3690,"sha256":"f99bca566fe4df715309b87ed7ec36dd69a6706ca7c3f6d1b8ae6c8123366676","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2460,"sha256":"39a07dddbad2534b1cbca48ed17b50e92064a74407d88920aabdd1e6417079c0","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789099672801,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"c42c55292311c8db405335ae67919e6da145a98133dde94aba16d42f3eff0087","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/c42c55292311c8db405335ae67919e6da145a98133dde94aba16d42f3eff0087","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1780085631902},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":18,"checkedAt":1789099672801},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill is a coherent file manager, but it needs Review because its bulk rename and sync commands can unexpectedly move or delete user files outside the intended scope.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The tools operate on arbitrary user-supplied directory trees and can copy, move, rename, or delete files; batch rename does not constrain generated names to the selected directory, and sync does not reject overlapping source and target roots.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No install hook, remote payload, external dependency, or package-install behavior was found; requirements.txt states standard library only.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The instructions cover broad file-management triggers and include delete, mirror, execute, no-confirm, and scheduled automation patterns without equally prominent scope limits or recovery guidance.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill does not install persistence or escalate privileges, but its best-practices document shows cron-style unattended execution and the rename script supports --no-confirm for bulk changes.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The artifact purpose matches file organization, renaming, duplicate cleanup, and sync scripts; however, size-based organization and bidirectional sync are advertised but only placeholders.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Review this skill carefully before installing. It has no network or credential behavior, but it can make broad local filesystem changes. Use scan-only or preview modes first, avoid --no-confirm and unattended cron usage, do not run sync with overlapping source and target directories, and prefer quarantine/move workflows over direct deletion until the path-scope issues are fixed.","findings":"[TP4] unexpected: Downgraded in part: the package does include rename, deduplicate, organize, and sync scripts, but some advertised features are not implemented.\n[AE1] unexpected: Overridden: artifact/scripts/sync.py was present and inspected fully enough for adjudication; no analysis-evasion behavior was found.\n[TM1] expected: Bulk renaming is purpose-aligned, but --execute --no-confirm creates a real unattended mass-change risk.\n[LP3] unexpected: Accepted as a Review concern: file access is expected, but the artifact does not define path boundaries for high-impact file mutations.\n[SQP-1] expected: Broad activation is consistent with a general file manager, but it compounds risk because the skill includes destructive and bulk operations.\n[SQP-2] expected: Delete, move, mirror, and execute examples are purpose-aligned but under-warned relative to their data-loss impact.\n[SQP-3] expected: Chinese-only user-facing text is visible and consistent across the artifact; treated as a usability and disclosure note, not a security escalation by itself.\n[EA2] expected: The no-confirm option supports automation but materially weakens human review for bulk filesystem changes.\n[SDI-4] unexpected: Accepted as a documentation mismatch: bidirectional sync is described but only prints an under-development message.\n[SDI-1] unexpected: Accepted as a capability mismatch for bidirectional sync; this is not malicious but should be corrected before users rely on it.\n[T09] unexpected: Accepted: batch rename constructs destinations from user-controlled name parts without validating they remain filenames, and its preview only shows basenames.\n[T09] unexpected: Accepted: mirror sync does not reject identical or overlapping source and target roots, so --delete can remove source files or nested targets can grow recursively.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789099672801}}}}}